        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/data/official-evals/infra-official-v1/corpus/cuda-asynchronous-concurrent-execution.md",
        "sha256": "6167d857cfa9fd78264f595af7ef8e0b2dc9add6720cf00c56f97e6cf12d8f28",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/data/official-evals/infra-official-v1/corpus/cuda-asynchronous-concurrent-execution.md#L21-L21",
        "content": "Concurrent host execution is facilitated through asynchronous library functions that return control to the host thread before the device completes the requested task.\nUsing asynchronous calls, many device operations can be queued up together to be executed by the CUDA driver when appropriate device resources are available.\nThis relieves the host thread of much of the responsibility to manage the device, leaving it free for other tasks.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "collection": "official",
          "document_id": "cuda-asynchronous-concurrent-execution",
          "url": "https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/13.0.1/cuda-c-programming-guide/index.html#asynchronous-concurrent-execution",
